<title>USA: Muni sales to total $2.2 bln for week of Jan 6.</title>
<headline>Muni sales to total $2.2 bln for week of Jan 6.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scheduled competitive and negotiated municipal bond sales for the week of Jan 6 have been updated and are now expected to total $2.2 billion in 80 offerings, according to Reuters Municipal Bond Information Group.</p>
<p>Competitive sales total $806 million in 53 issues. The largest is a $245.8 million two-part Washington general obligation deal on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Negotiated sales total $1.4 billion in 27 offerings. The largest is a $345.7 million Houston refunding deal through senior manager PaineWebber Inc.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Information Group, 212-859-1826</p>
</text>
